WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.796
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.996 --> 00:08.432
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.466 --> 00:11.785
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.819 --> 00:14.972
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:15.006 --> 00:18.409
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.444 --> 00:22.013
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:22.047 --> 00:23.581
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.615 --> 00:25.316
♪ Laugh and cry

00:25.351 --> 00:28.651
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.845 --> 00:39.208
♪ Everyone has fingernails

00:39.210 --> 00:40.977
♪ And everyone wants cash

00:41.012 --> 00:43.463
♪ So send us all
your fingernails ♪

00:43.497 --> 00:45.632
♪ And we'll send you
some cash ♪

00:45.666 --> 00:47.400
♪ Fingernails for cash
dot com ♪

00:47.435 --> 00:49.269
♪ Fingernails for cash

00:49.303 --> 00:51.638
♪ Remember it's just
fingernails ♪

00:51.673 --> 00:53.891
♪ So don't expect much cash

00:53.925 --> 00:55.893
♪ Fingernails for cash dot com

00:55.927 --> 00:57.895
♪ Our service never fails

00:57.929 --> 00:59.063
♪ Just take the cash

00:59.097 --> 01:00.398
♪ And don't ask why

01:00.432 --> 01:02.016
♪ We want your fingernails

01:02.050 --> 01:05.469
♪ 'Cause we might be building
a fort with them. ♪

01:11.343 --> 01:12.343
Here you go, fellas.

01:12.377 --> 01:13.344
Thanks, Horace.

01:13.378 --> 01:14.895
Oh, here, let me
get this one, Peter.

01:14.930 --> 01:18.049
Geez, what the hell kind of
stupid wallet is that, Joe?

01:18.083 --> 01:20.551
(sighs) Bonnie's
making wallets now.

01:20.585 --> 01:22.987
Look, she's gonna ask
you guys to buy one.

01:23.021 --> 01:24.472
I'll just give
you the money.

01:24.506 --> 01:25.774
Just don't throw it out

01:25.808 --> 01:28.627
within five miles
of where we live.

01:28.661 --> 01:30.729
Hey, why do you have a
Harvard dining hall I.D.?

01:30.763 --> 01:32.714
I pulled over some
punk Harvard kid

01:32.749 --> 01:35.183
who gave me a bunch of
lip, so I took his I.D.

01:35.218 --> 01:37.969
Man, I bet they got fancy food
up there at Harvard.

01:38.004 --> 01:39.888
Like them turkeys
with paper shoes.

01:39.922 --> 01:41.707
Or pigs with apples
in their mouths.

01:41.741 --> 01:44.159
Or them lambs what ain't never
seen the light before.

01:44.193 --> 01:46.128
Oh, yeah, I love
eating food that's sad.

01:46.162 --> 01:47.696
Hey, you know,
we should drive up there

01:47.730 --> 01:49.331
and use that card
to eat for free.

01:49.365 --> 01:50.565
That's a
great idea!

01:50.600 --> 01:51.917
Let's go
to Harvard!

01:51.951 --> 01:53.418
Oh, I don't know, you guys.

01:53.453 --> 01:55.654
We'll be as out of place there
as a black guy in Sweden.

01:56.589 --> 01:58.775
CROWD:
Ooh!

01:58.809 --> 02:00.042
Blackin sippin.

02:00.077 --> 02:02.328
Ya, blackin
sippin.

02:02.362 --> 02:04.380
♪

02:17.594 --> 02:19.312
Wow, so this
is it.

02:19.346 --> 02:20.980
Harvard
University.

02:21.014 --> 02:22.682
The alma mater
of Fred Grandy,

02:22.733 --> 02:24.333
Amy Brenneman
and Ted Kaczynski.

02:24.368 --> 02:26.869
Are we sure this is
the way to the dining hall?

02:26.904 --> 02:28.488
Oh, I'm sorry, are your feet
getting tired?

02:28.522 --> 02:31.441
God, I'd love to be able to
wheel around in a toy all day.

02:31.475 --> 02:33.193
Ah, this is
it, you guys.

02:33.244 --> 02:34.828
The Harvard
Dining Hall.

02:42.187 --> 02:43.470
Holy crap!

02:43.505 --> 02:44.671
This place
is amazing!

02:44.706 --> 02:47.391
And just think, this is
where Helen Keller

02:47.425 --> 02:48.992
used to eat
when she went here.

02:49.027 --> 02:51.562
Tonight, I want to go out
and just get wasted.

02:51.596 --> 02:53.163
And not one
of these campus bars.

02:53.198 --> 02:55.015
I want to get wrecked
by a townie.

02:55.049 --> 02:56.784
Helen, you're
outrageous.

02:56.818 --> 02:58.969
I can't believe you're
getting away with this.

02:59.003 --> 03:01.054
I've been getting away
with this since I was seven.

03:01.089 --> 03:03.273
Believe me, I know
what I'm doing.

03:03.308 --> 03:05.058
Good morning, girls.

03:05.093 --> 03:06.060
Helen.

03:06.111 --> 03:08.112
(moaning)

03:11.033 --> 03:14.285
No freaking way.

03:14.320 --> 03:15.787
They have breakfast for dinner.

03:15.821 --> 03:17.422
Lois never lets me do that!

03:19.425 --> 03:20.875
(line ringing)

03:20.910 --> 03:23.211
Lois, do you have any idea
what I'm looking at right now?

03:23.245 --> 03:24.996
LOIS: Peter, we're not
doing this again.

03:25.030 --> 03:26.331
I am at Harvard,

03:26.365 --> 03:28.405
the smartest school in
the country, and they have...

03:28.434 --> 03:30.735
Peter, breakfast
for dinner is anarchy.

03:30.769 --> 03:32.604
It's fun, Lois!
It's whimsical!

03:32.638 --> 03:33.605
It's ridiculous!

03:33.639 --> 03:35.440
Pancakes are not
a nighttime food.

03:35.474 --> 03:36.741
You're ridiculous!

03:36.775 --> 03:37.909
Boy, breakfast
for dinner is

03:37.943 --> 03:39.612
a real hot-button issue
for you guys, huh?

03:39.646 --> 03:41.547
She's also mad
'cause I shook Stewie

03:41.581 --> 03:43.048
and now he's
walking weird.

03:48.872 --> 03:51.440
<i>Hey, was Beowulf
a Teen Wolf sequel</i>

03:51.474 --> 03:53.075
with Scott Baio?
No.

03:53.109 --> 03:54.777
(sighs) Then I just
totally failed

03:54.811 --> 03:56.312
that Medieval Lit
midterm.

03:56.346 --> 03:57.847
So this is
a Harvard bar, huh?

03:57.881 --> 03:59.181
Seems pretty normal.

03:59.216 --> 04:00.249
Hey, check it out,

04:00.283 --> 04:02.017
there's the
Winklevoss twins.

04:02.052 --> 04:03.252
Let's get a drink.
Get a drink.

04:03.253 --> 04:04.870
Let's get a drink.
I thought of it first.

04:06.840 --> 04:08.290
Hey, you guys noticed
how many Asians

04:08.325 --> 04:09.291
there are at
this school?

04:09.326 --> 04:10.960
I mean, how'd they
all get so smart?

04:10.994 --> 04:13.396
I don't know. Guess that's just
the way God made 'em.

04:13.431 --> 04:14.931
Gentlemen, I give you...

04:14.966 --> 04:16.333
the Asian.

04:16.367 --> 04:17.601
Ooh...

04:17.635 --> 04:20.103
Compact, hairless
and fiercely intelligent.

04:20.137 --> 04:22.572
The penises, while tiny,
are extremely efficient.

04:22.607 --> 04:25.075
We're projecting ten billion
within five years.

04:25.109 --> 04:26.743
Also, there'll be
different varieties

04:26.777 --> 04:28.345
that will all hate each other
for some reason.

04:28.379 --> 04:30.447
Do they eat just,
like, regular food?

04:30.481 --> 04:32.515
(chuckling):
No, no, no, the opposite.

04:36.654 --> 04:38.655
♪

04:39.991 --> 04:41.725
All right, this
is more like it.

04:41.759 --> 04:44.194
Way better than that
lame-ass college joint.

04:44.228 --> 04:46.380
Yeah, finally
a terrible Boston bar

04:46.415 --> 04:47.999
with a giant low-def TV.

04:48.050 --> 04:49.500
Let's go, Celtics!

04:49.551 --> 04:51.135
<i>I think that's
The Dr. Oz Show.</i>

04:51.169 --> 04:52.420
What are you talking about?

04:52.454 --> 04:53.971
<i>This is the last scene
of Independence Day.</i>

04:54.006 --> 04:55.756
Hey, look, even
the bartender's low-def.

04:55.790 --> 04:57.758
Hey, what can I
get you fellas?

04:57.792 --> 04:59.176
Hey, what do you say
we get some shots?

04:59.227 --> 05:01.395
Yeah! Let's
get wasted!

05:01.430 --> 05:03.698
Yeah! Let's get
wicked bombed!

05:03.732 --> 05:06.467
Sorry, pal, we already have
an intense wheelchair guy.

05:06.485 --> 05:07.835
Well, now,
hold on, hold on.

05:07.869 --> 05:09.670
What's your name, friend?
Peter.

05:09.705 --> 05:11.422
Yeah, we already got
a wheelchair guy.

05:14.042 --> 05:16.027
♪

05:45.141 --> 05:46.558
♪

06:04.228 --> 06:05.428
Oh, hey, Stewie.

06:05.462 --> 06:09.032
Hey, sometimes when
daddies drive home drunk,

06:09.066 --> 06:11.567
they come from
far away places,

06:11.602 --> 06:14.671
but it's okay because
they didn't get arrested

06:14.705 --> 06:16.305
and they're still
kind of drunk

06:16.340 --> 06:17.874
so they-they think
it's okay.

06:17.908 --> 06:20.376
You should know that Mom
has emotionally let you go.

06:20.411 --> 06:22.745
It won't be long
before she takes a lover.

06:22.780 --> 06:24.280
Ah, my head!

06:24.314 --> 06:26.050
She already has
two cell phones.

06:26.084 --> 06:28.452
Aw, man, what happened
last night?

06:28.486 --> 06:30.621
WOMAN (gruff voice):
I can tell you what happened.

06:30.655 --> 06:32.356
What the...?
Who the hell are you?

06:32.390 --> 06:34.391
Who the hell do you
think I am, sweetie?

06:36.795 --> 06:38.612
Oh, no. You mean...?

06:38.646 --> 06:40.280
That's right, baby.

06:40.315 --> 06:42.716
As of last night,
we're man and wife.

06:42.751 --> 06:45.019
By the way, I need
you to call my pimp

06:45.053 --> 06:46.220
and tell him I quit.

06:46.254 --> 06:47.454
Oh, my God, I...

06:47.489 --> 06:49.223
I married a hooker?

06:49.257 --> 06:50.224
Married?

06:50.258 --> 06:52.059
All right,
bachelor party!

06:52.093 --> 06:53.961
Come on!
Back to Boston!

06:57.298 --> 06:58.833
Aw, aw, damn it.

06:58.868 --> 07:00.235
I guess we're not going.

07:00.286 --> 07:01.920
Hey, Stewie,
here's five bucks.

07:01.954 --> 07:03.154
Get naked.

07:09.779 --> 07:11.413
This... this can't be possible!

07:11.448 --> 07:13.148
I can't be married
to a prostitute!

07:13.183 --> 07:15.084
Where will you two be going
on your scummymoon?

07:15.118 --> 07:17.186
And can I plan your
bridal golden shower?

07:17.220 --> 07:18.454
I don't even know your name!

07:18.488 --> 07:20.723
It's Charmese.
Perfect.

07:20.757 --> 07:23.525
Listen, Charmese, I was
obviously very, very drunk.

07:23.560 --> 07:25.060
This whole thing
is a huge mistake.

07:25.095 --> 07:26.695
Now, we got to
fix this right away.

07:26.730 --> 07:28.597
Like hell we do,
sweet cream.

07:28.632 --> 07:30.532
This is just what
I've always wanted:

07:30.567 --> 07:32.235
to settle down,
find a husband

07:32.269 --> 07:33.670
and live the
married life.

07:33.704 --> 07:35.772
And now I got that.

07:35.806 --> 07:37.507
Your new wife
is a human toilet.

07:37.541 --> 07:39.793
Look, I don't remember
anything about last night.

07:39.827 --> 07:41.761
How do I... how do I even know
we're really married?

07:41.796 --> 07:44.064
I got our marriage certificate
right here.

07:45.066 --> 07:46.266
It's legit.

07:46.300 --> 07:48.251
And it looks like I signed
one of the witness lines

07:48.285 --> 07:50.086
and Peter partially signed
the other.

07:50.121 --> 07:51.154
(chuckles)

07:51.188 --> 07:52.188
Joe, look.

07:56.744 --> 07:59.863
You know, after 40 years
in my line of work,

07:59.897 --> 08:02.298
I've learned the difference
between true love

08:02.333 --> 08:04.984
and doing the entire bowling
team of a pizza restaurant

08:05.019 --> 08:06.587
on a box spring by a brook.

08:06.621 --> 08:08.489
This is true love.

08:08.523 --> 08:10.558
Hey, what's our
last name again?

08:14.696 --> 08:16.430
You know, Quagmire,
I was thinking last night,

08:16.465 --> 08:19.900
I might remember Charmese
from a stag party in 1991.

08:19.935 --> 08:21.902
Ask her if she remembers
getting hit in the forehead

08:21.937 --> 08:23.137
with a meatball sandwich.

08:23.171 --> 08:24.872
You guys, I can't
stay married to her.

08:24.906 --> 08:27.141
This whole thing
is a complete disaster!

08:27.175 --> 08:28.259
In fact, you know what?

08:28.293 --> 08:30.013
I got to go down
to the courthouse right now

08:30.045 --> 08:31.145
and file for divorce.

08:31.179 --> 08:32.580
This thing ends now.

08:32.614 --> 08:33.964
Hang on,
Quagmire.

08:33.999 --> 08:35.399
I'm not sure
that's a good idea.

08:35.434 --> 08:39.037
Quahog has some extremely
draconian laws governing divorce

08:39.072 --> 08:40.939
that all heavily
favor the woman.

08:40.973 --> 08:41.973
What? What do you mean?

08:42.008 --> 08:42.974
Well, to be honest,

08:43.009 --> 08:44.176
if you divorce her,

08:44.210 --> 08:46.344
she'll probably get
everything you have.

08:46.379 --> 08:47.946
What? No,
that's impossible!

08:47.980 --> 08:49.648
I can't lose all
my money and my house!

08:49.682 --> 08:51.116
Then I'll have
to move into some

08:51.150 --> 08:53.118
depressing divorced
guy apartment!

08:53.152 --> 08:54.553
As you can see,
we have plenty

08:54.587 --> 08:55.887
of cabinet space
for your plate.

08:55.922 --> 08:57.723
The oven, of course,
is just decorative.

08:57.757 --> 08:59.057
Seems okay.

08:59.092 --> 09:00.572
Do you have any other
units available?

09:00.593 --> 09:01.827
This is our only one.

09:01.861 --> 09:04.096
MAN (screaming):
I hope you're happy, Marsha!

09:04.130 --> 09:06.164
(thud) We might have
something upstairs.

09:06.199 --> 09:07.299
Sorry, Quagmire,

09:07.333 --> 09:08.633
but the only way
around the law

09:08.668 --> 09:10.268
is if the woman
consents to a divorce.

09:10.303 --> 09:11.570
Consent?

09:11.604 --> 09:13.039
But Charmese will
never agree to that.

09:13.073 --> 09:15.374
You heard her, the crazy skank
wants to be a wife.

09:15.409 --> 09:16.542
She's found
herself a husband

09:16.577 --> 09:17.543
and she's not
letting go.

09:17.578 --> 09:18.978
I bet she's what happens

09:19.012 --> 09:21.114
if you put a Hooters girl
in the microwave on "high."

09:21.148 --> 09:22.248
Well, the only
other choice

09:22.282 --> 09:23.850
is to let her take
all your money.

09:23.884 --> 09:25.518
(sighs) Well, I
obviously can't do that.

09:25.552 --> 09:27.272
I guess I'm just gonna
have to suck it up...

09:27.287 --> 09:29.305
Let her suck it up-- she's
the expert. Sorry, keep going.

09:29.339 --> 09:31.274
...and at least try to make
things work with Charmese.

09:31.308 --> 09:32.608
And who knows?

09:32.643 --> 09:34.277
Maybe it... maybe it
won't be that bad.

09:34.311 --> 09:36.546
After all, I liked her enough
to marry her last night.

09:36.580 --> 09:37.820
I must've seen
something in her.

09:37.848 --> 09:39.482
There you go, that's
the spirit, buddy.

09:39.516 --> 09:41.117
There's a little bit
of good in everyone.

09:41.118 --> 09:43.119
<i>Except that president guy
from The Hunger Games.</i>

09:43.153 --> 09:44.203
He was pretty bad.

09:44.271 --> 09:46.406
This year, in addition
to the Hunger Games,

09:46.441 --> 09:48.926
we're going to do
the Special Hunger Games.

09:48.960 --> 09:50.110
I'm Andy!

09:50.145 --> 09:51.595
I love
you, Andy!

09:51.629 --> 09:52.963
Come on,
guys, fight.

09:55.800 --> 09:57.367
So, Doc, I figured
if Charmese and I

09:57.402 --> 09:58.702
are gonna live
as man and wife,

09:58.736 --> 10:00.037
I ought to get
her checked out.

10:00.071 --> 10:02.239
Of course. Charmese,
when's the last time

10:02.273 --> 10:03.440
you had a pelvic exam?

10:03.475 --> 10:05.242
When was
the Missouri Compromise?

10:05.276 --> 10:07.110
Uh, I think 1821.

10:07.145 --> 10:09.112
Then I've never
had a pelvic exam.

10:09.147 --> 10:10.297
All right,
I'm going in.

10:10.331 --> 10:12.483
If I tug on the rope twice,
that means pull me out.

10:13.885 --> 10:16.453
(squishy footsteps)

10:16.488 --> 10:17.988
HARTMAN:
God, who are the pigs

10:18.022 --> 10:20.492
who just throw their
empty beer cans down here?

10:24.396 --> 10:25.363
Hey, Charmese.

10:25.397 --> 10:27.198
You know, I really
love your clothes...

10:27.232 --> 10:28.449
I found a lot of them

10:28.484 --> 10:30.351
on strung-out
teenage corpses.

10:30.386 --> 10:31.352
That's so lovely.

10:31.387 --> 10:32.948
But I was thinking,
maybe this afternoon

10:32.955 --> 10:34.455
you'd like to borrow
my credit card

10:34.490 --> 10:35.924
and buy yourself
a new wardrobe.

10:35.958 --> 10:37.725
You know, something
a little more conservative.

10:37.760 --> 10:38.726
Really?

10:38.761 --> 10:40.261
That's so
sweet, Glenn.

10:40.296 --> 10:42.564
No one's ever cared
about me like that before.

10:42.598 --> 10:44.165
Thank you.

10:44.200 --> 10:46.334
♪ Uptown girl

10:46.368 --> 10:49.754
♪ She's been living
in her uptown world ♪

10:49.788 --> 10:53.209
♪ I bet she never had
a backstreet guy ♪

10:53.243 --> 10:57.062
♪ I bet her mama
never told her why ♪

10:57.097 --> 11:01.283
♪ I'm gonna try
for an uptown girl ♪

11:01.318 --> 11:04.954
♪ She's been living
in her white bread world ♪

11:04.988 --> 11:08.290
♪ As long as anyone
with hot blood can... ♪

11:08.325 --> 11:10.242
I would like to pawn
all these clothes

11:10.277 --> 11:11.477
for crack money.

11:14.781 --> 11:16.916
Gosh, thanks so much
for having us over, you guys.

11:16.950 --> 11:18.517
Of course, Glenn.

11:18.552 --> 11:20.286
Welcome to our
home, Charmese.

11:20.320 --> 11:21.687
Sit anywhere you like.

11:21.721 --> 11:24.723
That chair with the garbage bag
taped over it looks pretty good.

11:26.177 --> 11:28.044
Meg, you look
pretty next to her.

11:28.079 --> 11:29.980
So, Charmese,

11:30.014 --> 11:31.748
I was thinking
of writing an article

11:31.782 --> 11:33.149
about you
for my school paper.

11:33.184 --> 11:35.719
Do you charge black guys
more or less?

11:35.753 --> 11:37.387
Hmm, that's a hard question
to answer.

11:37.421 --> 11:39.089
Most of them get a group rate.

11:39.123 --> 11:40.857
Come on, now,
let's not talk about work.

11:40.892 --> 11:41.992
It's a dinner party.

11:42.026 --> 11:44.210
Are you and Glenn
thinking about children?

11:44.245 --> 11:46.780
Unfortunately,
I can't have children.

11:46.814 --> 11:48.381
Oh, menopause?

11:48.416 --> 11:51.585
No, I got knifed
in the vagina one Christmas.

11:51.619 --> 11:53.620
Ah, the holidays
are always stressful.

11:53.654 --> 11:56.089
I have $3.74.

11:56.123 --> 11:57.674
Do something to me.

11:57.708 --> 11:59.076
(hawks, spits)

11:59.111 --> 12:00.444
I love you.

12:00.479 --> 12:02.997
I want to take you
away from all this.

12:03.031 --> 12:04.949
They're supposedly putting
an ice cream place

12:04.983 --> 12:06.651
where the shoe store was.

12:06.685 --> 12:08.803
Excuse me, Lois,
where's your bathroom?

12:08.837 --> 12:10.871
I got to check on
a whistling sound.

12:10.873 --> 12:13.774
Upstairs, to the left.

12:13.809 --> 12:17.178
Um, I'm obsessed
with Charmese.

12:20.649 --> 12:22.049
Hey.

12:22.084 --> 12:23.084
Let's do it.

12:23.118 --> 12:24.735
What? You mean, like sex?

12:24.770 --> 12:26.320
Yeah, and we
should go now.

12:26.355 --> 12:27.995
I just stuffed everything
back into place.

12:28.023 --> 12:29.457
Uh, you know, Charmese,

12:29.491 --> 12:31.158
I don't really think
I'm in the mood.

12:31.193 --> 12:32.728
What? You're never
in the mood.

12:32.762 --> 12:34.162
We've been married
two weeks,

12:34.197 --> 12:36.198
